---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import PageHeader from "../components/layout/PageHeader.astro";
---

<Layout title="Privacy Charter & Data Boundaries">
  <PageHeader
    title="Privacy Policy & Data Boundaries"
    badge="Zero-Knowledge Privacy Charter"
    description="Effective Date: 2026 • Architecture Specification V5.3 • Zero plaintext escrow on BYOS servers."
  />

  {/* Content */}
  <section class="py-8 px-6 max-w-4xl mx-auto">
    <div class="p-8 sm:p-12 rounded-3xl border border-[#E2DFD8] bg-white space-y-8 text-sm text-[#6F7173] leading-relaxed shadow-xs">
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-[#2B2C2D] flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="text-[#9E725F]">1.</span> Customer-Controlled Persistent Storage
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Persistent email messages, attachments, draft contents, and address books are uploaded directly to your designated cloud storage bucket (AWS S3, Google Drive, MinIO, or Cloudflare R2). Every persistent object is encrypted client-side. BYOS servers hold zero persistent customer mail data in plaintext.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="pt-6 border-t border-[#E2DFD8]">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-[#2B2C2D] flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="text-[#9E725F]">2.</span> Inbound Transient Processing Window
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Inbound email arriving over SMTP from the internet is processed transiently in memory for spam filtering, virus checking, and envelope encryption. Immediately upon successful delivery to your storage bucket, transient in-memory buffers are wiped. Plaintext message bodies are never written to disk or the central relational database.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="pt-6 border-t border-[#E2DFD8]">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-[#2B2C2D] flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="text-[#9E725F]">3.</span> Privacy-Preserving Search
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          When search indexing is enabled, keywords are blinded on your device before searching. The BYOS relational database stores only blind cryptographic hashes. The BYOS platform cannot correlate search queries to actual keywords or readable messages.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="pt-6 border-t border-[#E2DFD8]">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-[#2B2C2D] flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="text-[#9E725F]">4.</span> Operational Metadata
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          To maintain email delivery reliability and defend against denial-of-service or abuse, BYOS retains essential operational metadata:
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-3 space-y-1.5 list-disc list-inside text-xs text-[#6F7173]">
          <li>Account credentials (salted and stretched via Argon2id)</li>
          <li>Verified custom domain routing records and DKIM public keys</li>
          <li>Rate limiting counters in volatile Redis cache</li>
          <li>Administrative audit logs for security revocations and employee terminations</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="pt-6 border-t border-[#E2DFD8]">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-[#2B2C2D] flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="text-[#9E725F]">5.</span> Zero Third-Party Tracking
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          The BYOS website and web applications contain zero third-party advertising trackers, cross-site analytics beacons, or behavioral profiling scripts. All assets and fonts are served locally.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
